{{!-- Bonus GRIT-cell block (Фокус, renamed to "GRIT") — a flat total, no armor involved:
     a Character's own base pool (GOD.BASE_GRIT/system.baseGrit), or an NPC's GM-set
     NPCDataModel.gritMax. Shared by the Character and NPC sheets, and rendered standalone
     by #patchGritTrack() (actor-sheet.mjs/npc-sheet.mjs) so click/crack/repair/max-±
     actions can patch just this block instead of re-rendering the whole sheet.

     Guard is "has at least one box OR we're in edit mode" (not hasGrit alone) — an NPC
     with gritMax still at 0 has zero boxes to show, but edit mode still needs the block
     to exist so its own "+"/"-" (below) are reachable to raise it off 0 in the first
     place; outside edit mode with zero boxes there's nothing to click at all, so it's
     hidden. "-" clamps at 0 (actor-sheet.mjs's/npc-sheet.mjs's #onGritMaxSubtractClick),
     never rendered disabled at the floor — just a no-op past it, same as "+" has no
     rendered ceiling either. --}}
{{#if (or gritTrack.hasGrit editMode)}}
<div class="grit-track">
  <div class="wound-track-head">
    <span class="wound-track-label"><i class="grit-icon"></i> GRIT</span>
  </div>
  <div class="wound-marks">
    {{#each gritTrack.boxes as |box|}}
    <div class="grit-mark state-{{box.state}}" data-index="{{box.index}}" data-tooltip="{{box.title}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">
      <i class="grit-icon"></i>
      {{#if (eq box.state "cracked")}}<i class="fas fa-bolt grit-crack-badge"></i>{{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/each}}
    {{#if editMode}}
    <button type="button" class="grit-max-sub" title="Уменьшить максимум GRIT на 1">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-minus"></i>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="grit-max-add" title="Увеличить максимум GRIT на 1">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i>
    </button>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</div>
{{/if}}
